{"chunk_id": "9d98fb8d585d", "text": "This passage depicts the astonishing ferocity of Abhimanyu during the Kurukshetra battle. Surrounded by elite Kaurava warriors\u2014Kripa, Aswatthaman, Karna, Kritavarman, and others\u2014the young son of Arjuna fights with relentless skill. He kills several princes and even slays Vrihadvala, causing thousands of kings to flee in panic. His duel with Karna is especially intense, both warriors bloodied yet radiant in battle. Abhimanyu continues cutting down chariots, steeds, and warriors, demonstrating speed and mastery that amazes even his enemies. Drona himself praises the youth\u2019s unmatched agility and compares him to Arjuna, admitting no flaw can be found in his fighting. Recognizing they cannot defeat him fairly, the Kaurava leaders discuss strategy: they must first disable his bow and chariot. Acting on Drona\u2019s advice, Karna finally cuts Abhimanyu\u2019s bow, marking a crucial turning point that foreshadows the treacherous tactics soon to follow.\nAbhimanyu devastates Kaurava warriors, duels Karna and others, earns Drona\u2019s admiration, and prompts a plan to disarm and isolate him.\nThemes: heroic valor, youthful prowess, battle tactics, admiration of an enemy, encirclement strategy", "vector": [-0.021211085841059685, -0.010947021655738354, -0.0006119529716670513, 0.0009587673703208566, -0.018269114196300507, 0.041949354112148285, -0.02570284530520439, -0.010553007945418358, -0.02336503006517887, -0.024139923974871635, 0.018820734694600105, -0.00048636100837029517, 0.0030601753387600183, 0.004009092226624489, 0.000423154589952901, 0.012897390872240067, 0.04549548029899597, -0.011183430440723896, 0.017073938623070717, -0.02202538214623928, -0.005598281975835562, -0.001493148854933679, 0.0005434109480120242, 0.017678093165159225, -0.029472246766090393, 0.0331234410405159, 0.0010416745208203793, -0.031205907464027405, 0.016233375295996666, -0.032204076647758484, 0.0005159120773896575, -0.002162151737138629, 0.00528